      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/175/5857",
      "text": [
        " : \"مَا مِنْ أَحَدٍ اُبْتُلِيَ وَ إِنْ عَظُمَتْ بَلْوَاهُ بِأَحَقَّ بِالدُّعَاءِ مِنَ اَلْمُعَافَى اَلَّذِي لاَ يَأْمَنُ اَلْبَلاَءَ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5857 - Al-Hasan ibn Musa Al-Khashshab narrated from Ghiyath ibn Kallub, from Ishaq ibn Ammar, from Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as), from his forefathers, peace be upon them, that Imam Ali ibn Abi Talib (as), peace be upon him, used to say:\n\"There is no one afflicted with a trial, no matter how great his affliction, who is more deserving of supplication than the one who is in well-being and does not feel secure from tribulation.\""
        ]
      }
    },
